From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000123 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SacredTrees <121399723+SacredTrees@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 04:10:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] WebCore: a WebSocket with no channel fails, it does not
 assert

The Amiga port's pages are made with pageConfigurationWithEmptyClients(),
whose EmptySocketProvider gives a WebSocket no channel (patch 0071).
WebSocket::connect() then met RELEASE_ASSERT(m_channel): a page that did
new WebSocket(...) stopped the whole browser, its window dead (found in
the lab on 18 November 2026 with wss://echo.websocket.org).

With no channel the connection now fails cleanly: a console message,
then, after the constructor has returned, the error event and the close
event (not clean, code 1006), so a page's onerror and onclose run and
the page carries on, or falls back to another transport. WebKit's own
failAsynchronously() sends the error event alone; pages that wait for
close to fall back need both. Nothing changes where a channel exists.
---
 Source/WebCore/Modules/websockets/WebSocket.cpp | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Source/WebCore/Modules/websockets/WebSocket.cpp b/Source/WebCore/Modules/websockets/WebSocket.cpp
index 4803b8d5d..2e681a22a 100644
--- a/Source/WebCore/Modules/websockets/WebSocket.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebCore/Modules/websockets/WebSocket.cpp
@@ -300,6 +300,24 @@ ExceptionOr<void> WebSocket::connect(const String& url, const Vector<String>& pr
     if (RefPtr provider = context->socketProvider())
         m_channel = ThreadableWebSocketChannel::create(context.get(), *this, *provider);
 
+#if PLATFORM(AMIGA)
+    // The Amiga port gives a page no WebSocket channel yet
+    // (EmptySocketProvider, patch 0071): the connection fails after the
+    // constructor has returned, with the error event and then the close
+    // event (not clean, code 1006) that a page's fallback waits for, where
+    // the assertion below stopped the whole browser.
+    if (!m_channel) {
+        context->addConsoleMessage(MessageSource::JS, MessageLevel::Error, "WebSocket is not available in this browser yet"_s);
+        queueTaskKeepingObjectAlive(*this, TaskSource::WebSocket, [](auto& socket) {
+            socket.m_state = CLOSED;
+            socket.dispatchErrorEventIfNeeded();
+            socket.dispatchEvent(CloseEvent::create(false, ThreadableWebSocketChannel::CloseEventCodeAbnormalClosure, emptyString()));
+            socket.stop();
+        });
+        return { };
+    }
+#endif
+
     // Every ScriptExecutionContext should have a SocketProvider.
     RELEASE_ASSERT(m_channel);
 
